lued cards (Aces, 2s, Jokers) or gain the lead. Playing low cards like 7, 8, or J would allow the Landlord to easily regain control later or pass the burden to my teammate.\n\nReason: I hold a single ♠K, which is a disconnected card in my hand (I have pairs of 10s, Qs, and As). Playing the King serves two purposes: it acts as a strong blocker to force the Landlord to spend a high card (Ace or 2), and it optimizes my hand structure by removing a loose single. Keeping the Pair of Aces and the single 2 is crucial for future defense and control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠K"]}'}
